-- title:
--   Properness of regular hyperbolic twisted GL₂-orbit maps adelically
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $D$ be a datum [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28) for $(\mathcal{O}_L, K, L)$, that is, a monoid homomorphism $D.\mathrm{act}$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of the adèle ring $\mathbb{A}_L$, each of which is continuous and agrees with the given automorphism of $L$ on the image of $L$ under the structure map $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$; write $\sigma$ also for the induced entrywise automorphism [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14) of $G = \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$. Let $H \le G$ be a subgroup assumed to consist exactly of those $h \in G$ whose $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries vanish and for which $\sigma(h)h^{-1}$ lies in the centre of $G$. Let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ have vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries, and assume $N_{L/K}\big(\delta_0(0,0)/\delta_0(1,1)\big) \neq 1$. Then for every compact $C \subseteq G$ there is a compact $C' \subseteq G$ such that for all $y \in G$ and all idèles $z \in \mathbb{A}_L^{\times}$, if $y^{-1} \, \delta_0 \, \sigma\!\left(c(z)\,y\right) \in C$, where $\delta_0$ is viewed in $G$ entrywise through $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$ and $c(z)$ is the scalar matrix with entry $z$, then $y = hk$ for some $h \in H$ and $k \in C'$.
--
--   This is the properness statement for the twisted orbit map $y \mapsto y^{-1}\delta_0\sigma(y)$ attached to a regular hyperbolic (diagonal, with non-unit norm of the ratio of eigenvalues) element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, taken modulo the centre and modulo its twisted centraliser $H$. It is the support bound behind the convergence of hyperbolic twisted orbital integrals, and is used in the evaluation of the hyperbolic terms of the twisted trace formula, as in the integrability and integral-identity statements for such orbital integrals over $H \backslash G$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_isCompact_forall_exists_mem_mul_of_inv_mul_globalPoints_mul_sigmaAdelicAct_centralScalar_mul_mem_of_diagonal.lean

